# Offsite copies of the backups with restic (plan M9; docs/SICHERUNG.md, "Zeitplan,
# Aufbewahrung, Offsite"). Optional: copy to backup.env next to compose.yml; only the
# service backup reads it. Without HERD_BACKUP_OFFSITE_REPOSITORY the archives stay on
# the volume backups alone (offsite=off).
#
# The restic repository (created on the first run), e.g. s3:https://s3.example/bucket/herd,
# b2:bucket:herd, sftp:user@host:/srv/restic/herd or rest:https://host/herd.
# HERD_BACKUP_OFFSITE_REPOSITORY=
# Its password, required with a repository: `openssl rand -hex 32`. Keep it apart from
# the server: without it the offsite copies cannot be read.
# HERD_BACKUP_OFFSITE_PASSWORD=
# The storage's own credentials, passed to restic and nothing else (AWS_*, B2_*,
# AZURE_*, GOOGLE_*, OS_*, ST_*, RESTIC_* other than the repository and the password):
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
